  "name": "Thaitails",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Thaitails is an annual furry convention in Thailand, started by members of the Thai furry community who had visited overseas conventions and wanted a large gathering at home. The first was held January 30, 2016, in a meeting room at SCB Asok Towers in Bangkok with 125 attendees. It later moved to hotels in Bangkok and became a two-day event in 2019, and since 2024 it has been held at the Grand Richmond Hotel in Nonthaburi, passing 1,000 attendees. Each year has a theme and supports a wildlife charity, such as the Wildlife Friends Foundation Thailand and the Wild Animal Rescue Foundation of Thailand.",
